ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: green
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [NFKC vs NFD divergence is *exactly* the predicted mechanism — but "predicted by basic Unicode theory" is not a mundane-deflation here: the claim is empirical magnitude on real corpora, not theoretical novelty. The 95.1% is a measurement, not a model artifact. No mundane "it's just the LSH S-curve" escape: METRIC B shows 34.6% survive real MinHash@T=0.8, decoupling from exact-string artifact.]
CONFOUNDS: [GT-normalizer choice (NFKC+casefold) is the model-side definition itself, so circularity is structural to the claim, not a confound — harness-computed, never read by production normalizer (anti-circular control passes). Twin construction uses NFKC(d) which is the same operator as GT — but the claim is precisely "production misses NFKC-equivalents," so this is the operative definition, not a leak. Per-language variance (ar 55.6% vs zh 99.8%) is mechanistically explained by fullwidth-ASCII prevalence in CJK web, consistent with attribution table.]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [Assumption that "the model tokenizer" uses NFKC+casefold is treated as the pervasive multilingual default rather than measured against a specific loaded tokenizer.json — packet acknowledges this caveat; a pure-NFC tokenizer (e.g., Llama-family SentencePiece without NFKC) would shrink the gap substantially. The 95.1% is conditional on "model normalizer ⊇ NFKC+casefold," which holds for BERT-multilingual/XLM-R/mT5/GPT-2-style BPE+NFKC but NOT universally. Does not bound the harm: model-identical ≠ memorization-equivalent (training-loss equivalence under tokenizer normalization is asserted, not measured downstream).]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [No confidence intervals on per-language rates (n=587 for de, n=674 for ar — Wilson 95% CI for de 94.7% ≈ ±1.8%, still ≫1% gate, so no decision change). No bootstrap over doc sampling from C4 splits. No variance across MinHash seeds for METRIC B's 34.6% (single-seed banded LSH). Effect size so large (95× the gate) that statistical fragility is not load-bearing for the verdict.]
RATIONALE: Mechanism is predicted by Unicode spec (NFD is canonical-only by definition, structurally cannot collapse compatibility chars — Unicode Standard Annex #15 §1.2), so the *existence* of the gap is not surprising. What the L1 establishes is the **magnitude on real data**: 95.1% residual, 45.2% prevalence, 34.6% surviving real production MinHash. The mundane-theory deflation ("NFKC≠NFD, of course") would apply if the claim were "this gap exists" — but the claim is "the gap is operationally enormous in production pipelines, and no production tool closes it." The L1 measures the latter. The committee's own gate (≥1%) was set precisely to distinguish "theoretical curiosity" from "real exposure"; 95× clearance is not in the noise. The tokenizer-NFKC assumption is the only real caveat and is honestly flagged in the packet; it does not collapse the finding (NFKC+casefold is the dominant multilingual-tokenizer norm). No FATAL theory-side objection.
